+A web plugin whose browser half contributes a small badge to the host Session
+header, in the right-aligned utilities row beside the host's Session-log
+button. The host half only registers the lifecycle; the badge is a registered
+occupant of the declared `conversation.session.header.utilities` slot, and its
+copy belongs to the plugin's `bench-locale` locale dictionary.
+
+The first revision located the host button by matching its display text
+(`/session\s*log/i`). Host client copy became locale-owned in the 0.1.2
+client-locale rollout (rollup R-13), so the selector silently stopped matching
+on non-English locales — the injected badge disappeared with no error and no
+console exception — and the suggested second regex would only break again on
+the next language. Localized display text is never an identity, so the badge
+anchors to the slot declaration instead of to copy.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
